{"h":3395,"lines":[{"c":1,"w":0.072978350321451835,"x":0.83500253281859782,"h":0.014100428604826853,"t":"Reading","y":0.11264154449363317},{"h":0.017608469591264275,"t":"In 1866, he gave up his business to open a photographic studio, advertising himself as a portrait","x":0.1769244831808473,"w":0.71612848917643224,"c":1,"y":0.1525863922742805},{"x":0.17896288946373232,"w":0.71203018188476552,"t":"and landscape photographer. From about 1870 he dropped portraiture to specialize in landscape","h":0.015852946134281898,"c":1,"y":0.16836914044358675},{"x":0.17893203967828764,"y":0.18392962373950561,"c":1,"h":0.016443205385241799,"t":"photography and other views. His numerous photographs of city life revealed in street scenes,","w":0.69970799763997382},{"h":0.01472320376914027,"y":0.20053003552914839,"x":0.17901233740322853,"t":"houses, and markets are alive with human activity, and although his favourite subject was","w":0.66460906982421875,"c":1},{"y":0.21319404622423765,"h":0.01882316760095748,"x":0.17686819467568435,"w":0.68327616373697919,"c":1,"t":"landscape he usually composed his scenes around such human pursuits as farming the land,"},{"y":0.22940418352565839,"w":0.71209126790364585,"t":"cutting ice on a river, or sailing down a woodland stream. There was sufficient demand for these","x":0.17893092395658072,"h":0.015889097018292331,"c":1},{"t":"types of scenes and others he took depicting the lumber trade, steamboats and waterfalls to enable","y":0.24705535917609012,"c":1,"x":0.17901233631407534,"w":0.72839508056640634,"h":0.013250883392226132},{"c":1,"w":0.70793487548828116,"h":0.017723064400141597,"x":0.17690311471569772,"y":0.2612893221911039,"t":"him to make a living. There was little competing hobby or amateur photography before the late"},{"c":1,"w":0.68312759399414058,"t":"1880s because of the time-consuming techniques involved and the weight of the equipment.","y":0.27761627894985241,"x":0.17901233457132132,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.29358068337663101,"c":1,"x":0.17901235625360926,"w":0.70781890869140629,"t":"People wanted to buy photographs as souvenirs of a trip or as gifts, and catering to this market,","h":0.013250883392226132},{"y":0.30771243422708694,"w":0.69970367431640623,"x":0.17689981286941531,"t":"Henderson had stock photographs on display at his studio for mounting, framing, or inclusion","h":0.017852232228740661,"c":1},{"y":0.35453474698061038,"x":0.17695473303474121,"h":0.016195524146054296,"c":1,"t":"Henderson frequently exhibited his photographs in Montreal and abroad, in London, Edinburgh,","w":0.71810699462890626},{"x":0.17896296978370504,"y":0.36875825858343458,"h":0.016181636334027139,"c":1,"t":"Dublin, Paris, New York, and Philadelphia. He met with greater success in 1877 and 1878 in","w":0.68529673258463553},{"y":0.38500765816136306,"c":1,"t":"New York when he won first prizes in the exhibition held by E and H T Anthony and Company","x":0.17897188872837649,"w":0.7017352803548178,"h":0.015211502991800963},{"x":0.17695473586134636,"c":1,"y":0.40106007061677373,"h":0.016195524146054296,"t":"for landscapes using the Lambertype process. In 1878 his work won second prize at the world","w":0.69958847045898431},{"c":1,"x":0.17675881303644472,"y":0.41592942354915374,"h":0.014487660815774683,"w":0.14657099405924481,"t":"exhibition in Paris."},{"y":0.44579258367285313,"h":0.01757181996591517,"t":"In the 1870s and 1880s Henderson travelled widely throughout Quebec and Ontario, in Canada,","w":0.71613759358723961,"x":0.17485110690087519,"c":1},{"y":0.46183665653058303,"t":"documenting the major cities of the two provinces and many of the villages in Quebec. He was","w":0.70585871378580722,"h":0.015157702954834762,"c":1,"x":0.17896711216975716},{"x":0.176954744975374,"y":0.47819767428564508,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.69547322591145833,"c":1,"t":"especially fond of the wilderness and often travelled by canoe on the Blanche, du Lievre, and"},{"x":0.17896763726478962,"h":0.01390584983870613,"c":1,"y":0.49239960077968448,"t":"other noted eastern rivers. He went on several occasions to the Maritimes and in 1872 he sailed","w":0.70791656494140631},{"w":0.72643529256184902,"h":0.015088519443471449,"x":0.17897033767737525,"y":0.50842926383013076,"t":"by yacht along the lower north shore of the St Lawrence River. That same year, while in the lower","c":1},{"h":0.015353813328647492,"c":1,"y":0.52321082800925844,"w":0.68733510335286463,"x":0.17897412985088712,"t":"St Lawrence River region, he took some photographs of the construction of the Intercolonial"},{"w":0.70594726562499988,"y":0.53766667726148742,"t":"Railway. This undertaking led in 1875 to a commission from the railway to record the principal","h":0.01745045395706224,"x":0.17893713615430187,"c":1},{"h":0.015200612682616521,"c":1,"t":"structures along the almost-completed line connecting Montreal to Halifax. Commissions from","x":0.17894344090224051,"y":0.55451664137716872,"w":0.7079514058430989},{"t":"other railways followed. In 1876 he photographed bridges on the Quebec, Montreal, Ottawa and","h":0.017156915473713341,"y":0.56956945996125619,"x":0.17690014184833283,"w":0.71411834716796885,"c":1},{"y":0.58568904596050009,"w":0.68930043538411456,"x":0.17901233364316851,"h":0.013250883392226132,"c":1,"t":"Occidental Railway between Montreal and Ottawa. In 1885 he went west along the Canadian"},{"y":0.60026944787597836,"w":0.71616770426432297,"t":"Pacific Railway (CPR) as far as Rogers Pass in British Columbia, where he took photographs of","x":0.17690662737490395,"h":0.018470305857304581,"c":1},{"t":"the mountains and the progress of construction.","y":0.61773255801789329,"h":0.013081395583944611,"w":0.3539094543457032,"x":0.17901235090585213,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"In 1892 Henderson accepted a full-time position with the CPR as manager of a photographic","h":0.014563987898180808,"w":0.69341562906901044,"x":0.17489712413576228,"y":0.64680232543780247},{"c":1,"w":0.69354100545247399,"h":0.017585514010192371,"y":0.66128400707149448,"t":"department which he was to set up and administer. His duties included spending four months","x":0.1768959211076562},{"h":0.016046580212416672,"c":1,"w":0.68724278767903646,"t":"in the field each year. That summer he made his second trip west, photographing extensively","x":0.17695473789258984,"y":0.67726737341362153},{"y":0.69186046494612397,"c":1,"x":0.17695473723029381,"h":0.017503492402524912,"t":"along the railway line as far as Victoria. He continued in this post until 1897, when he retired","w":0.69341562906901033},{"t":"completely from photography.","c":1,"w":0.22839505513509115,"x":0.17695473571893369,"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.70930232544202421},{"t":"When Henderson died in 1913, his huge collection of glass negatives was stored in the basement","c":1,"h":0.016044868316470673,"y":0.73837209287424954,"x":0.17901235446185373,"w":0.72016459147135414},{"c":1,"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.75436046496720088,"w":0.71810699462890626,"t":"of his house. Today collections of his work are held at the National Archives of Canada, Ottawa,","x":0.17695473314864879},{"c":1,"h":0.017860513132227918,"y":0.77001913415756351,"w":0.43432927449544273,"t":"and the McCord Museum of Canadian History, Montreal.","x":0.17480962344836731},{"t":"This text is taken, for the most part, verbatim from the Dictionary of Canadian Biography Volume XIV (1911-1920). For design purposes,","c":1,"x":0.17896290417334407,"y":0.83343317262798156,"h":0.014078688986590704,"w":0.71203796386718743},{"h":0.016132371585697691,"x":0.17690095637267461,"w":0.70386133829752606,"t":"quotation marks have been omitted. Source: http:\/\/www.biographi.ca\/en\/bio\/henderson_alexander_1831_1913_14E.html. Reproduced","y":0.8441687966988829,"c":1},{"t":"with permission.","x":0.17658684460337715,"y":0.85699758476718046,"h":0.01209177313760823,"c":1,"w":0.089176781972249375},{"x":0.8827160489951833,"y":0.86627906953300604,"w":0.026748971939086874,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"t":"39"}],"w":2400}